Zero padding on each spatial side.  `"valid"` is no padding;
`"same"` keeps the spatial size, needs `stride=1`, and puts
the extra element of an odd total after.

notes:
Per-element loss:



$$
L_i = \begin{cases}
    \tfrac{1}{2}(x_i - y_i)^2 / \beta & |x_i - y_i| < \beta \\
    |x_i - y_i| - \tfrac{1}{2}\beta & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Continuously differentiable everywhere; gradient is
$(x_i - y_i)/\beta$ inside the quadratic region and
$\operatorname{sign}(x_i - y_i)$ outside.

Per-element loss:



$$
L_i = \begin{cases}
    \tfrac{1}{2}(x_i - y_i)^2 & |x_i - y_i| \le \delta \\
    \delta\,\big(|x_i - y_i| - \tfrac{1}{2}\delta\big) & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
$$

Unlike `smooth_l1_loss`, the quadratic region is *not*
rescaled by $1/\delta$, so the loss magnitude itself
grows with $\delta$.

