Per-element loss (constant-in-$x$ terms dropped):



$$
L_i = \begin{cases}
    e^{x_i} - y_i\,x_i & \text{log\_input = True} \\
    x_i - y_i \log(x_i + \varepsilon) & \text{log\_input = False}
\end{cases}
$$

Gradient w.r.t. $x$ is $e^x - y$ (log-input form)
or $1 - y/(x + \varepsilon)$ (rate form).  Both push
$\lambda$ toward $y$ in expectation.

parameters.description:
